Description: Fix LLVM-16 C++23/libc++ compatibility in SwiftShader
 In C++23 with libc++, std::unique_ptr's destructor is constexpr, which
 forces early instantiation requiring the complete type at class definition.
 This affects GlobalValueSummaryList and other LLVM types using unique_ptr.
 .
 Changes:
 - Replace unique_ptr with raw pointers where incomplete types cause issues
 - Add explicit destructors and out-of-line definitions
 - Update lambda signatures from unique_ptr references to raw pointers
 - Remove .get() calls on elements that are now raw pointers
 .
 Note: APFloat getFirst/getSecond getters, MIPatternMatch LLT parameter,
 and DiagnosticInfo templates are already fixed in Chromium 143 upstream.
 Only the destructor definition is needed for APFloat in this patch.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-12

